# Code owners — GitHub requests review from these owners on matching changes.
# To make this binding, enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the main
# branch protection rule. The supply-chain-critical paths below are the ones an
# attacker would target to subvert CI, releases, or dependency provenance.

# Default owner for everything.
*                       @juninmd

# CI/CD and release pipeline — a change here can run arbitrary code with the
# repo's GITHUB_TOKEN and publish/release artifacts.
/.github/               @juninmd
/.github/workflows/     @juninmd

# Dependency + supply-chain policy. Cargo.lock is the pinned dependency set;
# deny.toml is the allowlist gate; touching either changes what ships.
/Cargo.toml             @juninmd
/Cargo.lock             @juninmd
/deny.toml              @juninmd

# CI helper scripts execute in the runner.
/scripts/               @juninmd
